\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Morphism Chain End-to-End: Type Safety and S-Entropy Conservation through $\mathrm  {access} \circ \mathrm  {fuse} \circ \mathrm  {catalyze}^* \circ \mathrm  {observe}$.} (\textbf  {A})~Shannon entropy of the partition signature $\Sigma $ measured after each chain stage: observe, $\mathrm  {catalyze}^*$ (helix + cofactor kernels), and fuse. Entropy decreases by approximately 0.04 nats from observe to fuse, well within the theoretical bound of Theorem~8.2. (\textbf  {B})~Final $12 \times 12$ binary contact map output by access at threshold $\tau _c = \mathrm  {median}(\Sigma ) + 0.5\,\mathrm  {std}(\Sigma )$. The diagonal-dominant pattern with secondary-structure-like off-diagonal bands confirms the chain produces a structured contact prediction; density 0.06 is consistent with the helix-shifted prior. (\textbf  {C})~Comparison of the actual S-entropy change $|S_{\mathrm  {out}} - S_{\mathrm  {in}}|$ (green) against the theoretical bound $\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _k \ln |\mathcal  {K}_k| + N^2 H(\tau _c) + \mathfrak  {S}_{\mathrm  {floor}}$ (red). The actual value is two orders of magnitude below the bound, confirming the chain is conservative under the stated kernels. (\textbf  {D})~Three-dimensional surface rendering of the binary contact map over the residue index plane $(i, j)$, with elevated ridges marking contacting pairs. The diagonal mass and secondary-structure off-diagonal protrusions render the morphism chain's output as a tangible structural prediction, closing the receiver evaluation $\mathrm  {eval}_{\mathcal  {R}_{\mathrm  {bio}}}: \mathcal  {T}(\xi _{\mathrm  {biomolecule}}) \to \mathrm  {Structure}_{N \times N}$.}}{10}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:morphism_chain}{{4}{10}{\textbf {Morphism Chain End-to-End: Type Safety and S-Entropy Conservation through $\mathrm {access} \circ \mathrm {fuse} \circ \mathrm {catalyze}^* \circ \mathrm {observe}$.} (\textbf {A})~Shannon entropy of the partition signature $\Sigma $ measured after each chain stage: observe, $\mathrm {catalyze}^*$ (helix + cofactor kernels), and fuse. Entropy decreases by approximately 0.04 nats from observe to fuse, well within the theoretical bound of Theorem~8.2. (\textbf {B})~Final $12 \times 12$ binary contact map output by access at threshold $\tau _c = \mathrm {median}(\Sigma ) + 0.5\,\mathrm {std}(\Sigma )$. The diagonal-dominant pattern with secondary-structure-like off-diagonal bands confirms the chain produces a structured contact prediction; density 0.06 is consistent with the helix-shifted prior. (\textbf {C})~Comparison of the actual S-entropy change $|S_{\mathrm {out}} - S_{\mathrm {in}}|$ (green) against the theoretical bound $\sum _k \ln |\mathcal {K}_k| + N^2 H(\tau _c) + \mathfrak {S}_{\mathrm {floor}}$ (red). The actual value is two orders of magnitude below the bound, confirming the chain is conservative under the stated kernels. (\textbf {D})~Three-dimensional surface rendering of the binary contact map over the residue index plane $(i, j)$, with elevated ridges marking contacting pairs. The diagonal mass and secondary-structure off-diagonal protrusions render the morphism chain's output as a tangible structural prediction, closing the receiver evaluation $\mathrm {eval}_{\mathcal {R}_{\mathrm {bio}}}: \mathcal {T}(\xi _{\mathrm {biomolecule}}) \to \mathrm {Structure}_{N \times N}$}{figure.caption.5}{}}
